<cell id="cell-0"><cell_type>markdown</cell_type># M9 L9: RAG End-to-End

**Compose the M5-M8 primitives into a full RAG pipeline.**

Duration: 90 min.  No API keys.</cell id="cell-0>
<cell id="cell-1"><cell_type>markdown</cell_type>## Plain English (the 12-year-old version)

**RAG** (Retrieval-Augmented Generation) is the production pattern for "answer questions about a private document collection."

The recipe: when the user asks a question, **search** the documents for the most relevant paragraphs, **paste** them into the prompt, and ask the AI to answer using only those paragraphs. This is the difference between "AI knows what the internet knew in 2021" and "AI knows your company's 2024 policies."</cell id="cell-1>
<cell id="cell-2"><cell_type>markdown</cell_type>## The 5 things to know

1. **RAG is composition** -- ingest (M5) + chunk (M6) + embed (M3) + retrieve (M7) + prompt (M8).
2. **The four seams that bite**: ingestion, chunking, retrieval, prompt.
3. **Context cap** -- typically 2K-4K chars; longer dilutes signal and increases cost.
4. **Retrieval is the most common failure** -- fix with a reranker (M7).
5. **Always measure on a golden set** -- retrieval recall@K, end-to-end answer quality, cost, latency.</cell id="cell-2>
